BT 1 0 0 1 0 63.3 Tm /F1 8.7 Tf 12 TL (A student activity record first arrives through the platform API or user interface. The input layer checks that the student ID and) Tj T* (course ID are valid, required fields are present, timestamps are valid and the score/activity value is within the accepted range.) Tj T* (A valid record receives a unique record ID and is stored in the persistent record store. Its ID is inserted into a hash-table index) Tj T* (for expected constant-time exact lookup. If the record requires expensive analytics, a background job is created and inserted) Tj T* (into a min-heap using \(priority, arrival sequence\). The scheduler repeatedly extracts the most urgent job. Completed records) Tj T* (are collected into a report batch, sorted by score or activity ID, and exported.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 54.18898 595.1969 cm
q
BT 1 0 0 1 0 39.3 Tm 12 TL /F2 8.7 Tf 0 0 0 rg (Correctness constraints:) Tj /F1 8.7 Tf ( \(1\) reject duplicate unique IDs; \(2\) never index a record before successful validation/storage; \(3\)) Tj T* (preserve referential integrity between student and course IDs; \(4\) a hash collision must not overwrite another key; \(5\) heap) Tj T* (ordering must use priority and then arrival sequence; \(6\) sorting must preserve all duplicate values; \(7\) report generation must) Tj T* (use a consistent input snapshot.) Tj T* ET
Q
