BT 1 0 0 1 0 39.3 Tm /F1 8.7 Tf 12 TL (The structures solve different access patterns. A hash table maps a key to a record and is optimized for exact-match lookup) Tj T* (and insertion. A heap exposes only the minimum-priority job efficiently; it does not provide fast arbitrary ID lookup. Combining) Tj T* (them avoids forcing one structure to perform an operation for which it is poorly suited. A separate job-ID hash index can) Tj T* (additionally support cancellation or status lookup.) Tj T* ET
