BT 1 0 0 1 0 39.3 Tm /F1 8.7 Tf 12 TL (Primary clustering occurs when contiguous occupied runs grow; new keys that hash into a run tend to extend it. Quadratic) Tj T* (probing uses offsets such as 1\262, 2\262, 3\262 to reduce primary clustering, but may not visit every slot for all capacities. Double) Tj T* (hashing uses a second hash function to choose the step size and generally distributes probe sequences better, provided the) Tj T* (step is relatively prime to table capacity.) Tj T* ET
